{"id":1951,"date":"2020-12-14T09:16:13","date_gmt":"2020-12-14T17:16:13","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1951"},"modified":"2024-09-01T13:57:20","modified_gmt":"2024-09-01T20:57:20","slug":"zumi-python-intermediate-driving-commands","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/zumi-python-intermediate-driving-commands\/","title":{"rendered":"1.5: Intermediate Driving Commands"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22151488df3\" name=\"6a22151488df3\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Intermediate Driving Commands<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered\">\n<div class=\"inner_cell\">\n<div class=\"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html\">\n<p>You know basic drive commands, but there are many driving maneuvers that cars need to perform other than go forward, reverse, left, and right. The Zumi library has many of these shapes and other commands programmed for you so that Zumi can operate just like a real self-driving car!<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"Import-libraries\">Import libraries<\/h3>\n<p>In [ ]:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">from zumi.zumi import Zumi\r\nimport time\r\nzumi = Zumi()<\/pre>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22151489037\" name=\"6a22151489037\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Drive functions<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-size: medium;\">Remember when you learned about\u00a0<span style=\"font-family: Courier;\">forward()<\/span>? Even though it set Zumi to drive at a set speed of 40 for one second in the current direction, you could also change these values. The function all listed below are all listed with their default parameters. If you call a function by name, such as\u00a0<span style=\"font-family: Courier;\">right_u_turn()<\/span>, Zumi will do the u-turn with the defined parameters. However, just like with\u00a0<span style=\"font-family: Courier;\">forward()<\/span>, you can change these to whatever values you would like.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">right_u_turn(speed=30, step=4, delay=0.02)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li>speed: the forward speed you want Zumi to drive at<\/li>\n<li>step: the angle step size as it goes from (0 &#8211; 180)<\/li>\n<li>delay: the delay between each angle step<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1954&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">left_u_turn(speed=30, step=4, delay=0.02)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li>speed: the forward speed you want Zumi to drive at<\/li>\n<li>step: the angle step size as it goes from (0 &#8211; 180)<\/li>\n<li>delay: the delay between each angle step<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1955&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">circle(speed=30, step=2, direction=1, delay=0.02)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li>speed: the forward speed you want Zumi to drive at<\/li>\n<li>step: the angle step size as it goes from (0 &#8211; 360)<\/li>\n<li>direction: -1 for clockwise , +1 for counterclockwise<\/li>\n<li>delay: the delay between each angle step<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1956&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">right_circle(speed=30, step=2)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li>speed: the forward speed you want Zumi to drive at<\/li>\n<li>step: the angle step size as it goes from (0 &#8211; 360)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1957&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">left_circle(speed=30, step=2)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li>speed: the forward speed you want Zumi to drive at<\/li>\n<li>step: the angle step size as it goes from (0 &#8211; 360)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1958&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">square(speed=40, seconds=1, direction=1)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li>speed: the forward speed you want Zumi to drive at<\/li>\n<li>seconds: the duration Zumi will drive for each side<\/li>\n<li>direction: -1 for clockwise , +1 for counterclockwise<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1959&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">square_right(speed=40, seconds=1.0)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li>speed: the forward speed you want Zumi to drive at<\/li>\n<li>seconds: the duration Zumi will drive for each side<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1960&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">square_left(speed=40, seconds=1.0)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li>speed: the forward speed you want Zumi to drive at<\/li>\n<li>seconds: the duration Zumi will drive for each side<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1961&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">j_turn(speed=100, step=4, delay=0.005)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li>speed: the forward speed you want Zumi to drive at<\/li>\n<li>step: the angle step size<\/li>\n<li>delay: the delay between each angle step<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1962&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">figure_8(speed=30, step=3, delay=0.02)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li>speed: the forward speed you want Zumi to drive at<\/li>\n<li>step: the angle step size as it goes from (0 &#8211; 360)<\/li>\n<li>delay: the delay between each angle step<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1963&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">parallel_park(speed=15, step=1, delay=0.01)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li>speed: the forward speed you want Zumi to drive at<\/li>\n<li>step: the angle step size as it turns<\/li>\n<li>delay: the delay between each angle step<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1964&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">rectangle(speed=40, seconds=1.0, direction=1, ratio=2)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li>speed: the forward speed you want Zumi to drive at<\/li>\n<li>seconds: the duration Zumi will drive for the shorter side<\/li>\n<li>direction: -1 for clockwise , +1 for counterclockwise<\/li>\n<li>ratio: the ratio of the longer side to the shorter side<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1965&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">triangle(speed=40, seconds=1.5, direction=1)<\/pre>\n<ul>\n<li>speed: the forward speed you want Zumi to drive at<\/li>\n<li>seconds: the duration Zumi will drive for each side<\/li>\n<li>direction: -1 for clockwise , +1 for counterclockwise<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1966&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Let&#8217;s see an example of these in action!<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"python\">zumi.figure_8() # Runs figure 8 at default values\r\ntime.sleep(1)\r\nzumi.figure_8(speed = 50) # Changing one value\r\ntime.sleep(1)\r\nzumi.figure_8(step=4, delay=0.03) # Changing two values\r\ntime.sleep(1)\r\nzumi.figure_8(speed=40, step=4, delay=0.03) # Changing all three values<\/pre>\n<p>Test out some of these drive functions in the cell below. Just know that as you change the parameters, you may need more space. We recommend that you drive Zumi on the floor and keep an eye on it while it\u2019s driving.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 3 Intermediate Driving Commands [vc_column_text] You know basic drive commands, but there are many driving maneuvers that cars need to perform other than go forward, reverse, left, and&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/zumi-python-intermediate-driving-commands\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":2050,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":810,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[2135,2232,2156,2122,2134,2230],"class_list":["post-1951","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-beginner","lesson-tag-drive-commands","lesson-tag-intermediate","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-python","lesson-tag-zumi","module-beginner","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"h